<title>GERMANY: German airports flown cargo up 5.2 pct Jan-Oct.</title>
<headline>German airports flown cargo up 5.2 pct Jan-Oct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total air cargo flown to and from Germany rose 5.2 percent to 1,623,931 tonnes over the first ten months of 1996, the monthly traffic report of the German airports association (ADV) said.</p>
<p>The following table shows total,flown and trucked air cargo volumes in tonnes at international German airports January-October 1996 with percentage changes from a year ago.</p>
<p> AIRPORT	     FLOWN   TRUCKED  TOTAL    % CHANGE</p>
<p> Berlin (total)    26,265   4,783   31,048    +9.7</p>
<p> - Tegel	     15,463   4,499   19,962   +10.4</p>
<p> - Tempelhof	    284	 0	284   -50.1</p>
<p> - Schoenefeld     10,518     284   10,802   +12.1</p>
<p> Bremen		 2,149  20,063   22,212   +16.5</p>
<p> Dresden		1,199   2,431    3,630   +20.9</p>
<p> Duessseldorf	47,210     n/a	n/a</p>
<p> Frankfurt	1,121,177     n/a	n/a</p>
<p> Hamburg	     30,243     n/a	n/a</p>
<p> Hannover	     8,913     n/a	n/a</p>
<p> Cologne	    264,402  26,936  291,338   +11.1</p>
<p> Leipzig/Halle	2,528   1,204    3,732   +49.2</p>
<p> Munich		65,709     n/a	n/a</p>
<p> Muenster/Osnabrueck  563  10,290   10,853   +10.4</p>
<p> Nuremberg	   37,384  25,471   62,855    +8.2</p>
<p> Saarbruecken	   715   1,354    2,069    -0.3</p>
<p> Stuttgart	   15,474  44,580   60,054    +4.3</p>
<p> TOTAL	    1,623,931     n/a     n/a</p>
<p>*Notes: No overall air cargo total is given because several large airports with known large trucking volumes including Frankfurt, Munich and Duesseldorf do not release trucking figures. - Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
